&lt;header&gt;&lt;h1&gt;What’s new&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;p class="version"&gt;con 0.1.0-beta.183 · 2026-11-17&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/header&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Fixed&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Updates&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Add a persistent &lt;strong&gt;Automatically Check for Updates&lt;/strong&gt; switch in Settings → General → Updates. Turning it off stops background checks while keeping manual checks available. Show the actual checking preference instead of the ambiguous “Auto-update enabled” status.&lt;span class="credit"&gt;PR &lt;a href="https://github.com/nowledge-co/con-terminal/pull/565"&gt;#565&lt;/a&gt; by &lt;a href="https://github.com/wey-gu"&gt;@wey-gu&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Changed&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Updates&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Require an explicit installation decision for each con-managed release. macOS no longer offers silent automatic downloading or installation; portable updates retain separate download and restart actions. Package-managed installations continue using their original update mechanism.&lt;span class="credit"&gt;PR &lt;a href="https://github.com/nowledge-co/con-terminal/pull/565"&gt;#565&lt;/a&gt; by &lt;a href="https://github.com/wey-gu"&gt;@wey-gu&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
